NwOS F5 integration — build additions

1. Compile and link these kernel-side compiler sources:
   sys/kernel/nwc/nwc_runtime.c
   sys/kernel/nwc/lexer.c
   sys/kernel/nwc/parser.c
   sys/kernel/nwc/codegen.c
   sys/kernel/nwc/nwc_kernel.c

2. Compile and link:
   sys/kernel/Apps/textredactor/textredactor.c

3. Keep the normal host compiler files under compiler/ unchanged.
   compilerMain.c remains the Windows/host CLI compiler.

4. Replace/merge the filesystem block using kernel_fs_large_block.c.txt
   into the current sys/kernel/kernel.c.

5. The new filesystem uses:
   - 16 file slots
   - 32 sectors per file
   - 16384-byte maximum binary file size
   - 16383-byte maximum text file size

6. After the first boot with the new filesystem layout:
      NwOS> format
   This is required because the old one-sector-per-file layout is no longer compatible.

7. Text editor:
      F5 -> compile current editor contents -> write <name>.nwo
   The generated .nwo is binary, so fs_write_bytes() is used instead of fs_write().
